page();h('5. Prior art, chronology and what remains open')
p('The parent investigation compared the exact source with Tanner’s bit-oriented spectral argument [2], Zhu–Chugg’s regular-graph stopping bound [3], the original lifted-product construction [4], and quantum Tanner constructions [5]. Zhu–Chugg’s expression N(2γ−s)/(γk−s) uses a different threshold and has no small/large-support branch; it does not supply parameters making the source test useful. Constituent Ramanujan expansion is not a certificate for the expanded H<sub>X</sub> singular-value condition. The parent prior-art ledger includes inspected hypotheses, public GitHub code and accessible X posts, failed searches and full-text gaps. No global absence or priority claim follows from those bounded searches. The impossibility result follows from the proof above.')
p('Separate checked follow-ups establish stopping distance six for the B1 positive 63-multiple cyclic-cover family and classify the base matrix’s 441 size-six supports as unique companion Z-check rows. Those completed results use incidence information; they do not make Proposition 5.1 informative. They remain in the preceding incidence and classification artifacts. No additional paper or source question was encountered during this scope clarification.')
