p('<b>Question answered.</b> Can parameters in the paper’s stated positive-dimensional binary biregular scalar-factor QC-GHP model make Proposition 5.1 improve the stopping-distance guarantee beyond two? No: Theorem 1 proves nonexistence for every such parameter choice. The shared inventory records this as the fifth completed canonical Lean target (5/135); earlier checkpoint manifests retain their dated four-target counts. If “informative” means only the raw strict spectral inequality, the dense example instead gives a positive answer; it supplies no useful improvement. <b>Question still open.</b> A generally useful stronger replacement or tightening of the bound. The original canonical parameter question is marked answered negatively; the stronger-bound direction remains separately open. <b>Next proposed target (follow-up).</b> Prove an incidence-conditioned replacement that improves on two on a sparse family beyond the already completed B1 results.','Small2')
